      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults in a monitored setting. The usual over-the-counter limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nTypical adult oral regimens are:\n- **400 to 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours as needed**, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day. This is the usual range for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg/day or less**, divided into 3 or 4 doses, for mild to moderate pain.\n\nYou may have meant 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily. Or you may have meant 800 mg three or four times daily.\n\nPlease also have the treating prescriber confirm the intended dose, or enter the order themselves. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, and a pharmacist will likely review this one.\n\nIf you send me the confirmed dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. Please include the indication and any duration limit you want in the order note."
      }
